## Golden rules
<!-- Copy from .agents/rules/project-rules.md, plus the stack rules: -->
1. Branch per change; never push to `main`; never force-push; squash-merge after CI is green.
2. Tests for every change; root-cause bugs with a regression test.
3. A data field change touches model + admin schema + security rules + seed + tests together.
4. Never commit secrets. Never run destructive data scripts without the owner's explicit OK.
5. Docs (memory bank + documentation/ + ADR) in the same PR.

## Commands
```bash
# install, analyze, test, build, rules tests, seed dry-run
```

## Workflow
Branch from up-to-date `main` → change + tests + memory bank + documentation → PR (draft → ready) →
`@coderabbitai review` / `@sentry review` → fix findings, reply, resolve → CI green on head → squash-merge →
`main` auto-deploys → verify the deploy run and the live site → report.
Agents with the hark-workflow kit: start with the `hw-start` skill (or the `parent-agent` agent).

